    "source": "unblob integration fixtures, git LFS content path at tag 26.6.4",
    "why": "R42-C2 legacy classes need v1-v3 SquashFS inputs.  No writer in the lane emits v1-v3 (tools/round-39/gen-squashfs.py writes 4.0 only), and a hand-built v3 image would be a lane artifact rather than a third-party input.  These fixtures are MIT-licensed, 320-4096 B, and never a C1 carrier (plans/round-42-claims.md, reserved carriers).",
    "commit_plan": "commit the pinned copies under corpus/evidence/round-42/c2/fixtures/ (same `file` names) and pass --fixtures-dir; without them the generator needs --fetch",
    "damage_recipe": "damage_offset/damage_len mark a 4-byte zero window that makes sasquatch 4.5.1 fail with P=0 (root chunk) or fail and be carved (non-root chunk).  Every window was verified with REA 6.5.0 in round-42 wave 1; --verify re-checks the resulting envelope."
  },
